    "body": "Hello we are building a bot where we get personally identifiable information from the user. Hence we need to make sure that this data is not saved in any way on any Microsoft database. Hence We are currently building our own BotState (StateApi) to connect our personal DB instead of the default Azure one available out of the box.\r\n\r\nWhen we connect to our Bot using Direct Line Apis using the following steps:\r\n\r\n1) The DirectLineApi posts message to the bot using  userConversations.PostMessage(conversationId, msg)\r\n    ----> This hits our custom BotState source code as expected.\r\n\r\n2) But when we call userConversations.GetMessages(conversationId), --> It does not seem to invoke our BotState code. But the messages have appeared on the client side.\r\n\r\n3) We also tried closing down this connection and tried to call the userConversations.GetMessages(conversationId) after 2 minutes. It again seem to have not invoked our code, but have the messages appear to the user.\r\n\r\nThis gives us a feeling our messages are further stored somewhere in Hub (probably directline.botframework.com?) which is a concern for us. Could someone please throw some light on if and how the messages are stored in the hub inspite of us overriding the BotState?\r\n\r\nAlso how does watermark work when the BotState does not seem to have anything to do with watermarks.\r\nuserConversations.GetMessages(conversationId, waterWark.ToString());",
